  "editorial": "The high school sports students actually list on activities forms (specs/chances/inputs-beyond-academics.md, U12): every sport the NFHS High School Athletics Participation Survey counts under a state athletic association, plus the common club sports where schools field teams without state-association sanction (crew, ultimate, equestrian, esports, and similar). `org` names the sport's national governing body when one exists (USA Track & Field, USA Fencing, …), else the National Federation of State High School Associations (NFHS), whose member associations run the sport at the school level; `source_url` is that body's own site. One entry per sport regardless of which teams a state fields separately by sex. Aliases are the short forms students actually type (\"XC\", \"T&F\").",
